I'll take this too.

1088
01:04:21,930 --> 01:04:23,070
Wait, that's new?

1089
01:04:24,690 --> 01:04:25,250
Sprues!

1090
01:04:25,650 --> 01:04:26,210
Wow!

1091
01:04:27,810 --> 01:04:29,350
Can't believe I haven't found that yet.

1092
01:04:31,150 --> 01:04:32,450
Actually, I'll take this bell.

1093
01:04:35,970 --> 01:04:36,470
Thanks.

1094
01:04:37,750 --> 01:04:38,890
Nah, you can have it.

1095
01:04:41,130 --> 01:04:41,970
Don't want that.

1096
01:04:45,880 --> 01:04:47,120
Kids jumping on the bed.

1097
01:04:47,600 --> 01:04:48,100
Classic.

1098
01:04:54,800 --> 01:04:56,040
Okay, not bad.

1099
01:04:59,650 --> 01:05:00,150
Potatoes.

1100
01:05:00,350 --> 01:05:01,710
I guess we can make baked potatoes.

1101
01:05:05,630 --> 01:05:06,930
Not really feeling that.

1102
01:05:16,600 --> 01:05:17,120
Damn.

1103
01:05:17,720 --> 01:05:19,480
Well, it is what it is.

1104
01:05:20,040 --> 01:05:22,700
So the pumpkin pie just gave me four food.

1105
01:05:25,000 --> 01:05:27,600
Pumpkin pie is just as good as meat, it seems.

1106
01:05:28,400 --> 01:05:29,760
It may be on the level of steak.

1107
01:05:33,100 --> 01:05:34,140
Okay, let's head into a cave.

1108
01:05:38,170 --> 01:05:41,790
And let's not forget, I have gone west so far, so the way to get home is east.

1109
01:05:51,940 --> 01:05:53,340
Oh, I see iron already.

1110
01:05:54,020 --> 01:05:58,460
The problem is, I have a silk touch pickaxe, but it's actually not a problem.

1111
01:06:00,920 --> 01:06:04,280
We can make a stone pickaxe, or even an iron pickaxe, very soon.

1112
01:06:05,940 --> 01:06:06,800
Yeah, let's do that.

1113
01:06:07,020 --> 01:06:09,420
Ah, but to do that, I need a stone pickaxe first.

1114
01:06:09,420 --> 01:06:10,620
It sounds really dumb, but I do.

1115
01:06:16,920 --> 01:06:18,040
Make some of this.

1116
01:06:27,350 --> 01:06:27,910
Wait, what?

1117
01:06:30,050 --> 01:06:31,110
Why can't I make stone?

1118
01:06:32,210 --> 01:06:34,110
It needs to be cobblestone!

1119
01:06:34,710 --> 01:06:36,150
I can't even grab that.

1120
01:06:36,710 --> 01:06:37,650
That's wild.

1121
01:06:38,030 --> 01:06:38,750
What about andesite?

1122
01:06:45,680 --> 01:06:46,580
Brother, man.

1123
01:06:47,800 --> 01:06:49,240
Okay, there's a way we can do this.

1124
01:06:50,940 --> 01:06:53,660
I actually started hating silk touch.

1125
01:06:53,880 --> 01:06:55,420
I'm not even... like, this silk touch sucks!

1126
01:07:00,800 --> 01:07:02,760
I'm on team anti-silk touch.

1127
01:07:04,880 --> 01:07:07,120
Okay, now, stone pickaxe.

1128
01:07:08,880 --> 01:07:09,480
Finally.

1129
01:07:09,960 --> 01:07:12,560
And with the stone pickaxe, we can get an iron pickaxe.

1130
01:07:12,680 --> 01:07:14,680
We're going through all the different materials here.

1131
01:07:19,300 --> 01:07:20,600
Did I just throw away the wrong one?

1132
01:07:20,740 --> 01:07:21,280
God damn it!

1133
01:07:24,320 --> 01:07:24,860
Here we go.

1134
01:07:27,200 --> 01:07:28,140
Grab some of this.

1135
01:07:29,460 --> 01:07:33,140
That way we can actually cook the iron we find, so we can make an iron pickaxe.

1136
01:07:39,680 --> 01:07:47,160
In a world of create like this, I'm out here mining with a goddamn stone pickaxe.

1137
01:07:47,560 --> 01:07:49,700
You know how humiliating that is?

1138
01:07:53,760 --> 01:07:55,900
Burn!

1139
01:07:57,090 --> 01:07:57,640
Nice.

1140
01:07:59,030 --> 01:08:00,340
I see that up there.

1141
01:08:04,430 --> 01:08:06,100
That right there is my pickaxe.

1142
01:08:10,640 --> 01:08:11,330
Got it.

1143
01:08:13,210 --> 01:08:15,470
Now to make a furnace.

1144
01:08:16,710 --> 01:08:17,890
I'm gonna grab this.

1145
01:08:19,550 --> 01:08:19,890
Cobblestone.

1146
01:08:24,460 --> 01:08:25,400
I forgot how many I need.

1147
01:08:25,480 --> 01:08:26,120
Like, eight or something?

1148
01:08:37,690 --> 01:08:38,030
Iron.

1149
01:08:38,310 --> 01:08:39,670
And then we can make a pickaxe.

1150
01:08:39,750 --> 01:08:41,350
And then we are rolling.

1151
01:08:56,700 --> 01:08:58,620
In case I need to make a couple torches or something.

1152
01:09:10,290 --> 01:09:11,150
There we go.

1153
01:09:13,010 --> 01:09:13,790
It's time.

1154
01:09:17,830 --> 01:09:18,590
We got it.

1155
01:09:20,270 --> 01:09:21,790
The means to mine.

1156
01:09:23,950 --> 01:09:25,310
And let's go into the mine.

1157
01:09:27,290 --> 01:09:28,330
Things are looking up.

1158
01:09:31,040 --> 01:09:31,860
Uh, oh shit.

1159
01:09:32,560 --> 01:09:33,460
I can't think.

1160
01:09:34,420 --> 01:09:34,740
Brett.

1161
01:09:35,220 --> 01:09:36,040
That's the one I need.

1162
01:09:53,740 --> 01:09:55,340
Playing it so safe right now.

1163
01:09:58,430 --> 01:10:01,050
Man, their shooting cadence is so high.

1164
01:10:05,130 --> 01:10:06,090
More iron.

1165
01:10:07,870 --> 01:10:09,550
Dude, this is the perfect cave so far.

1166
01:10:10,090 --> 01:10:11,010
For what I need.

1167
01:10:18,200 --> 01:10:22,980
Also, someone did point out that apparently the creative tracks aren't really playing.

1168
01:10:23,320 --> 01:10:28,060
So I need to confirm that I've actually activated this mod that I installed.

1169
01:10:29,480 --> 01:10:30,600
I may have fucked it up.

1170
01:10:31,840 --> 01:10:33,360
Either that or I'm just very unlucky.

1171
01:10:37,690 --> 01:10:39,310
Because I do want to hear those tracks, you know?

1172
01:10:47,820 --> 01:10:48,480
More iron?

1173
01:10:48,640 --> 01:10:49,320
I love this cave.

1174
01:10:52,900 --> 01:10:53,160
Oh!

1175
01:10:53,400 --> 01:10:54,880
Uh, diamonds is also something we need.

1176
01:10:55,080 --> 01:10:56,740
But we gotta go a little deeper for that.

1177
01:10:57,420 --> 01:10:59,200
I just want to get my share of iron first.

1178
01:10:59,920 --> 01:11:00,900
Look at all these enemies here!

1179
01:11:00,960 --> 01:11:02,320
This is like a whole fucking harem.

1180
01:11:05,740 --> 01:11:07,860
The gang hideout has been located.

1181
01:11:08,140 --> 01:11:08,940
Actually, I have a bow.

1182
01:11:10,360 --> 01:11:10,880
I think.

1183
01:11:11,020 --> 01:11:11,500
Where's my bow?

1184
01:11:12,500 --> 01:11:13,120
I can't!

1185
01:11:13,520 --> 01:11:14,640
I want the time pressure!

1186
01:11:14,940 --> 01:11:15,420
There it is.

1187
01:11:20,850 --> 01:11:21,910
Is the bow even better?

1188
01:11:22,830 --> 01:11:23,670
It feels shit.

1189
01:11:25,550 --> 01:11:26,450
What's with these spiders?

1190
01:11:26,530 --> 01:11:27,070
Why are they drunk?

1191
01:11:29,290 --> 01:11:29,690
Fuck!

1192
01:11:29,910 --> 01:11:30,170
Oh no!

1193
01:11:30,570 --> 01:11:30,850
Oh no!

1194
01:11:31,410 --> 01:11:32,350
I may be in trouble!

1195
01:11:42,180 --> 01:11:43,340
Jesus fucking Christ!

1196
01:11:48,080 --> 01:11:49,780
Being stuck in a hole like that?

1197
01:11:49,860 --> 01:11:50,180
No good.

1198
01:11:54,140 --> 01:11:55,120
Good thing I have my armor.

1199
01:11:57,580 --> 01:11:58,700
Okay, okay.

1200
01:11:59,480 --> 01:12:00,100
Everything's fine.

1201
01:12:00,960 --> 01:12:02,940
I don't want this disgusting coal ore!

1202
01:12:03,860 --> 01:12:04,180
Ew!

1203
01:12:06,080 --> 01:12:07,560
Get this out of my face!

1204
01:12:09,660 --> 01:12:12,500
Actually, a string is something I do need a little bit of, but...

1205
01:12:13,040 --> 01:12:14,500
I don't want to go down there and pick it up.

1206
01:12:16,980 --> 01:12:18,220
I'll take this instead.

1207
01:12:22,880 --> 01:12:24,620
Only four loaves of bread left.

1208
01:12:29,260 --> 01:12:31,400
I do wish I had Lempa's bread right now.

1209
01:12:37,410 --> 01:12:38,750
Nothing exciting over there.

1210
01:12:38,890 --> 01:12:39,950
No iron for moi?

1211
01:12:44,690 --> 01:12:46,350
Um, I don't think I need zinc.

1212
01:12:48,050 --> 01:12:48,990
Not currently.

1213
01:12:51,370 --> 01:12:52,330
Give me more coal.

1214
01:13:01,960 --> 01:13:02,880
There we go!

1215
01:13:03,760 --> 01:13:05,200
And we gotta go deeper anyway.

1216
01:13:12,820 --> 01:13:13,900
Should I just do it?

1217
01:13:23,080 --> 01:13:23,480
Attack!

1218
01:13:25,840 --> 01:13:27,480
Too bad I didn't have the hammer, huh?

1219
01:13:29,040 --> 01:13:30,280
Could have done some damage.

1220
01:13:33,790 --> 01:13:36,110
Oh, look at this massive deposit of iron here.

1221
01:13:37,870 --> 01:13:38,870
There's even more!

1222
01:13:42,160 --> 01:13:42,560
Huge!

1223
01:13:49,260 --> 01:13:52,120
This cave is so much better than the other cave I have at home.

1224
01:13:59,760 --> 01:14:00,780
So far, at least.

1225
01:14:03,220 --> 01:14:04,500
Could be diamonds down there.

1226
01:14:15,780 --> 01:14:19,080
Man, iron pickaxes are really good.

1227
01:14:19,740 --> 01:14:20,920
Like, they're solid, you know?

1228
01:14:21,000 --> 01:14:22,140
They last a long time.

1229
01:14:22,900 --> 01:14:24,040
It's not too slow.

1230
01:14:24,040 --> 01:14:25,680
It's not super fast, of course, but...

1231
01:14:26,080 --> 01:14:27,780
But what it is, it's really good.

1232
01:14:34,000 --> 01:14:35,900
Iron pickaxes deserve your respect.

1233
01:14:36,200 --> 01:14:37,120
That's what I'm saying.

1234
01:14:39,160 --> 01:14:40,040
I'm going down.

1235
01:14:41,620 --> 01:14:42,140
Oh!

1236
01:14:42,400 --> 01:14:43,180
Massive iron!

1237
01:14:43,760 --> 01:14:45,800
I see it, but I also see danger.

1238
01:14:46,920 --> 01:14:48,020
How do I approach this?

1239
01:14:53,320 --> 01:14:53,960
What's up, brother?

1240
01:14:57,340 --> 01:14:57,700
Cute!

1241
01:15:25,720 --> 01:15:26,540
Explode then, I don't care.

1242
01:15:35,580 --> 01:15:36,940
Don't like all those creepers.

1243
01:15:38,460 --> 01:15:39,760
They could end me right now.

1244
01:15:46,740 --> 01:15:47,740
Yeah, okay, why not?

1245
01:15:49,240 --> 01:15:49,580
Oi!

1246
01:15:49,800 --> 01:15:50,360
That was a whole pool.

1247
01:15:54,540 --> 01:15:56,240
Now that's what I'm talking about!

1248
01:15:57,140 --> 01:15:58,720
Look at all those goodies!

1249
01:16:02,730 --> 01:16:03,630
My ankles.

1250
01:16:04,790 --> 01:16:05,670
Oh, yeah!

1251
01:16:06,550 --> 01:16:07,930
Oh, there's more!

1252
01:16:09,110 --> 01:16:10,850
We're gonna make a diamond pickaxe right now.

1253
01:16:12,910 --> 01:16:13,870
Maybe down here.

1254
01:16:15,370 --> 01:16:16,910
Make sure no enemies are spawning.

1255
01:16:18,150 --> 01:16:19,750
I want to be left in peace.

1256
01:16:26,750 --> 01:16:27,770
We're still back.

1257
01:16:29,590 --> 01:16:30,730
Get rid of this crap.

1258
01:16:31,690 --> 01:16:33,650
I will never touch iron again.

1259
01:16:33,850 --> 01:16:34,410
It sucks.

1260
01:16:39,440 --> 01:16:40,720
I think I also need more of this.

1261
01:16:41,120 --> 01:16:42,240
I'm running low on redstone.

1262
01:16:48,990 --> 01:16:49,990
I'll take some gold, too.

1263
01:16:51,310 --> 01:16:53,050
This is a fucking Schlaraffenland!

1264
01:16:53,870 --> 01:16:54,910
And I'm all here for it.

1265
01:16:58,940 --> 01:17:03,900
Now, there was one time when I was down here, and I was having a good time, and then all of a sudden I just got blown up.

1266
01:17:04,160 --> 01:17:05,300
No warning, no nothing.

1267
01:17:05,300 --> 01:17:09,140
A creeper from the freaking air just fell down on me and exploded on me.

1268
01:17:10,180 --> 01:17:13,420
So let's keep in mind that something like that could happen.

1269
01:17:15,300 --> 01:17:16,600
I'm gonna be extra careful.

1270
01:17:27,910 --> 01:17:28,630
More redstone.

1271
01:17:29,890 --> 01:17:30,770
Don't mind if I do.

1272
01:17:43,790 --> 01:17:45,010
Now, what else do I need?

1273
01:17:45,490 --> 01:17:47,030
Do I even need more diamonds?

1274
01:17:52,200 --> 01:17:53,640
I actually forgot why I came here.

1275
01:17:54,900 --> 01:17:56,300
It was just mainly iron, right?

1276
01:17:57,760 --> 01:18:00,260
I needed iron so I could make pressed iron.

1277
01:18:00,380 --> 01:18:00,860
Right, that's why.

1278
01:18:02,280 --> 01:18:05,660
And then I wanted to get diamonds anyway, since I was going mining.

1279
01:18:16,170 --> 01:18:19,230
And maybe we can even enchant a pickaxe today, if we get to 30.

1280
01:18:23,210 --> 01:18:24,890
You look so silly with no shirt on.

1281
01:18:34,820 --> 01:18:36,460
So far, this place has been magnificent.

1282
01:18:49,770 --> 01:18:50,810
That's my last bread.

1283
01:18:51,990 --> 01:18:55,550
But I do have a furnace, and I can cook this meat, so I'm gonna do it.

1284
01:18:56,810 --> 01:18:58,170
I'm gonna play this so safe.

1285
01:18:59,150 --> 01:19:00,650
And good thing we have lava over here.

1286
01:19:00,750 --> 01:19:02,150
That means easy deletion.

1287
01:19:08,770 --> 01:19:10,010
I'll keep the leather.

1288
01:19:12,950 --> 01:19:14,750
The rest is whatever.

1289
01:19:26,200 --> 01:19:27,100
Where are my sticks?

1290
01:19:27,100 --> 01:19:30,000
I mean, my... oh, my coal is here, of course.

1291
01:19:31,600 --> 01:19:33,000
I'll make a couple more torches.

1292
01:19:36,520 --> 01:19:37,040
64.

1293
01:19:39,420 --> 01:19:40,820
And then we have some meat now.

1294
01:19:41,420 --> 01:19:42,160
Things are looking up.

1295
01:19:46,560 --> 01:19:47,760
I just unlocked something.

1296
01:19:48,340 --> 01:19:48,800
Painting.

1297
01:20:01,930 --> 01:20:02,570
What's up, guys?

1298
01:20:04,010 --> 01:20:04,850
How's it hanging?

1299
01:20:13,510 --> 01:20:14,550
Go even deeper.

1300
01:20:15,970 --> 01:20:16,890
Should I, though?

1301
01:20:18,250 --> 01:20:18,770
Ow.

1302
01:20:26,820 --> 01:20:27,680
I smell diamonds.

1303
01:20:37,970 --> 01:20:39,090
I'm trying not to panic.

1304
01:20:39,250 --> 01:20:39,610
I'm just...

1305
01:20:39,610 --> 01:20:40,430
I'm just...

1306
01:20:40,430 --> 01:20:41,310
I'm just handling it.

1307
01:20:55,800 --> 01:20:57,660
I actually keep thinking of, um...

1308
01:20:58,740 --> 01:20:59,280
Oh, wait.

1309
01:20:59,360 --> 01:20:59,760
There's my thing.

1310
01:21:00,540 --> 01:21:00,980
Okay.

1311
01:21:01,380 --> 01:21:03,740
Why did it sound like my shield was breaking just now?

1312
01:21:04,000 --> 01:21:04,800
Did you hear that sound?

1313
01:21:10,510 --> 01:21:12,670
I keep thinking of ADHD, you know?

1314
01:21:13,010 --> 01:21:18,090
Like, if I actually have it, what it would feel like to get the medicine, you know?

1315
01:21:23,030 --> 01:21:28,970
Like, I keep thinking of the movie Limitless, because someone once told me that it's like taking the pill from Limitless, you know?

1316
01:21:30,190 --> 01:21:31,930
And that sounds fucking crazy to me.

1317
01:21:32,170 --> 01:21:32,630
Like, I...

1318
01:21:33,650 --> 01:21:37,350
Part of me kind of wants to have ADHD and then have the pill taken and then have that feeling.

1319
01:21:39,650 --> 01:21:41,930
Obviously, it's probably best if I don't have it, so I don't know.

1320
01:21:43,650 --> 01:21:44,890
What is even happening here?

1321
01:21:48,600 --> 01:21:50,000
Dude, I'm playing this masterfully?

1322
01:21:54,080 --> 01:21:55,280
There we go.

1323
01:21:55,740 --> 01:21:59,140
It was masterful until I said masterfully and then it became not masterfully.

1324
01:22:03,940 --> 01:22:05,020
Oh my god, bro!

1325
01:22:05,900 --> 01:22:06,620
Get away from me.

1326
01:22:07,440 --> 01:22:08,400
You also have an Enderman here.

1327
01:22:09,820 --> 01:22:10,800
I will kill him.

1328
01:22:21,480 --> 01:22:22,180
Come at me!

1329
01:22:22,340 --> 01:22:23,180
I've got NADP.

1330
01:22:26,960 --> 01:22:28,260
Sounds like some kind of disease.

1331
01:22:37,160 --> 01:22:41,940
Okay, next time we go mining, I will bring bottles of vision.

1332
01:22:43,460 --> 01:22:44,760
A vision enhancer.

1333
01:22:47,120 --> 01:22:48,800
Potion of foresight, whatever, you know what I mean.

1334
01:22:50,080 --> 01:22:50,680
See in the dark.

1335
01:23:01,690 --> 01:23:02,090
Gimme.

1336
01:23:06,880 --> 01:23:08,200
Okay, now check it out.

1337
01:23:09,400 --> 01:23:11,420
I am too damn greedy, know when to stop.

1338
01:23:11,540 --> 01:23:12,420
I know when to stop.

1339
01:23:13,880 --> 01:23:14,800
And it's right now.

1340
01:23:14,900 --> 01:23:15,480
We're stopping now.

1341
01:23:16,080 --> 01:23:18,020
Because I only have one piece of food left.

1342
01:23:18,580 --> 01:23:19,820
We got what we came for.

1343
01:23:20,380 --> 01:23:21,060
We're good.

1344
01:23:23,660 --> 01:23:24,600
I'm a changed man.

1345
01:23:24,680 --> 01:23:25,160
Never mind, there's more.

1346
01:23:26,940 --> 01:23:30,140
I mean, if they come at me like that, I take them, you know.

1347
01:23:31,340 --> 01:23:31,960
Let's go up.

1348
01:23:38,270 --> 01:23:38,870
Here we go!

1349
01:23:39,130 --> 01:23:41,630
Guys, it's going to be day, because today is a good day.

1350
01:23:42,410 --> 01:23:43,850
And it's not a good day if it's night.

1351
01:23:44,530 --> 01:23:45,050
You know why?

1352
01:23:45,690 --> 01:23:47,090
Because it'd be a good night instead.

1353
01:23:50,130 --> 01:23:51,390
